106: # ---- ppcrlwimiwidth: X(rlwimi) at 32-bit width + the wrapping mask's high half --------
107: # BEFORE the NetBSD prerequisite ON PURPOSE.  These rows are register-to-register on
108: # `-E bareppc -M 64` and need no image; behind need_file a missing image would turn a
109: # red detector into a silent SKIP.  Placed here, a red row is recorded first, and #371's
110: # gate_skip then reports FAIL rather than absorbing it.  PARSE BEFORE SCORE: gates grep
111: # the result line, never the exit status, and a missing or DUPLICATED protocol line is a
112: # FAIL.  Both halves of the score are pinned to a literal so a shrunk table cannot pass.
113: RLWLOG=$LOGDIR/ppc_rlwimi.log
114: python3 ppc_rlwimi_probe.py "$PMAX" gate > "$RLWLOG" 2>&1 || true
115: #  Each KEY must occur exactly once in ANY form, and that one line must be well formed --
116: #  counting only well-formed lines let a malformed EXTRA `RESULT=' through (codex review).
117: rlwres=$(grep -c '^PPC_RLWIMI_RESULT=' "$RLWLOG")
